Alongside <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a>, Apple today released iOS 26.7, an update to the existing <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-26/">iOS 26</a> software. Users who check for new software will see iOS 26.7 as the default update, with &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj; listed as an option at the bottom of the Software Update interface.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/ios-26-7.jpg" alt="" width="1672" height="941" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1064904" /><br/>
According to Apple's release notes, iOS 26.7 includes security fixes, but it does not have any other features. <br/>
<br/>
Apple will eventually show &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj; as the main update for the iPhone, but that likely won't happen for a few weeks. Users who want to stay on &zwnj;iOS 26&zwnj; for the time being can do so by opting for iOS 26.7 instead of &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj;.  <br/>
